LocalNodeNotLeader=The local cluster member is not a leader
InvalidAppendIndex=Committed log entry cannot be overwritten
SnapshotDetected=The method cannot be used for snapshot installation
RangeTooBig=The requested range is too big
UnexpectedError=The unexpected exception occurred
UnsupportedAddressFamily=Unsupported endpoint address family
UnavailableMember=Member is not reachable through the network
UnknownCommand=Command with id {0} cannot be recognized by the interpreter
MissingCommandId=Log entry must have associated command identifier
MissingMessageName=Message must have associated type and name
LeaderIsUnavailable=Leader node is not yet elected
UnknownRaftMessageType=Unknown Raft message type {0}
ConcurrentMembershipUpdate=Cluster membership cannot be modified concurrently
StreamRejected=The stream has been rejected by the server due to overflow of its backlog
ConnectionClosed=The underlying connection is closed
ConnectionTimedOut=The data cannot be sent or received on time
BadProtocolVersion=Multiplexing protocol version is not supported: {0}
BadCheckpointVersion=Checkpoint file version is not supported: {0}
LogEntryHashMismatch=Log entry hash doesn't match
MissingWalPage=WAL page {0} doesn't exist on the disk
StateMachineIsNotRestored=State machine is not restored. Call RestoreAsync first.
ConfigurationEntryNotReplicable=A configuration entry cannot be replicated directly. Use AddMemberAsync or RemoveMemberAsync to change the cluster membership.
ConfigurationManagedByCluster=The log belongs to a running cluster that derives its configuration from the log. Use AddMemberAsync or RemoveMemberAsync to change the cluster membership.
SnapshotRestoreCanceled=Restoring the state machine from the snapshot was canceled after it started. The state machine can be partially restored.
SnapshotInProgressCanceled=The snapshot that is being created by the state machine was canceled, so the snapshot received from the leader cannot be installed without reopening the state machine.
PayloadLengthMismatch=The payload has {0} bytes but its declared length is {1} bytes
InvalidMemberCount=The cluster configuration declares an invalid number of members: {0}
TruncatedConfiguration=The cluster configuration contains fewer members than it declares
EntriesCountMismatch=The request declares {0} log entries but only {1} were received
